            <div xml:id="d841">

                <pb facs="0717" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/2525</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 843</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-05">July 5, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        12.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that by Decree 1036 of May 30, 1940, the Government of Colombia guarantees such
                    obligations as the Bank of the Republic may contract from the Export-Import Bank
                    under the maximum $10,000,000 line of credit extended to that organization. The
                    Ministry of Finance and Public Credit is authorized to sign on behalf of the
                    Nation so as to make this guarantee of record. Copy of the original text,
                    together with translation, of the aforementioned decree are enclosed
                        herewith.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d841-f1"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spruille Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
